    rdf:value """Monday, March 19, 1906
Cloudy - a little rain.
Motored to Siena in Mr. Platt’s “Fiat”, only 1 hr. 48 m. going, 1 hr. 52 m. returning!
Perkins and the photographer Mr. Lavery also went.
Lunched with Mrs. Payne and Christina and Mr. Harvey.
Saw poor Platt’s pictures - an awful lot. Coming back very beautiful.
Wrote Mother, Mr. Britten, Emily, Miss Freeman, Mrs. Hooker, Miss Priestley.
Tuesday, March 20, 1906
Clouds, hail, snow, rain.
Placci came to lunch – boring - Hutchins called after - ditto - Mr. Fagan called, then nice Mr. Templeman Coolidge of Boston and Mrs. Middlemore. Then I went to town with Hutchins. Riri came to dine to talk about Oxford, and B.B. took him over to see Sir William Markby.
Wrote Mother, Emily, Mr. Cannon, Mrs. Whitehead, Contessa Serristori.
Wednesday, March 21, 1906
Cloudy.
Ray and Karin. They arrived at 6.30 looking very sweet. Alas Karin’s  other  ear is___ing and she is a good deal worried about it, and also she is very deaf. It is terrible.
Algar dined here, and the Hapgoods came in later.
Wrote Mother, Dr. Heath, Feliciangeli."""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 60 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1906> .

